.TH "HED" "1" "2026-08-23" "hed v1.21.3" "hed manual"
.SH NAME
hed \- A small sized(<1MB), hackable terminal editor written in C.
.PP
A small sized(<1MB), hackable terminal editor written in C.
.PP
Modal by default, but ships Emacs and VSCode keymaps you can swap to at
runtime.
Tree\-sitter highlights, ripgrep / fzf integrations, window splits, tmux
runner pane, OSC 52 clipboard, LSP.
Every user\-facing feature is a plugin you can rip out, fork, or
replace.
.PP
   *   *   *   *   *
.SH Install in 10 seconds
One line install:
.IP
.EX
curl \-fsSL https://github.com/42dotmk/hed/releases/latest/download/install.sh \f[B]|\f[R] bash
.EE
.PP
and follow the prompts.
.PP
The installer asks two things:
.IP "1." 3
\f[B]Source or binary?\f[R] Binary is faster (one download, ready to
run).
Source clones the repo into \f[CR]\[ti]/.local/share/hed\f[R], builds
it, and symlinks \f[CR]hed\f[R] and \f[CR]tsi\f[R] into
\f[CR]\[ti]/.local/bin\f[R] \[em] pick this if you want to hack on
plugins (or the core editor itself).
.IP "2." 3
\f[B]Optional tools?\f[R] Offers to download portable static
\f[CR]fzf\f[R] and \f[CR]ripgrep\f[R] binaries into the same
\f[CR]\[ti]/.local/bin\f[R], then lets you pick tree\-sitter grammars to
install for syntax highlighting.
.PP
No \f[CR]sudo\f[R].
No package manager.
Everything ends up under \f[CR]\[ti]/.local/\f[R].
.PP
After install, make sure \f[CR]\[ti]/.local/bin\f[R] is on your
\f[CR]PATH\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
export PATH=\[dq]$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH\[dq]
.EE
.PP
and
.PP
Then run \f[CR]hed\f[R] and you\[cq]re in.
.PP
   *   *   *   *   *
.SH Build from source manually
If you want to skip the installer:
.IP
.EX
git clone \-\-recursive https://github.com/42dotmk/hed.git

cd hed

make
.EE
.PP
\f[CR]make\f[R] only compiles.
It builds two binaries into \f[CR]build/\f[R]:
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[CR]build/hed\f[R] \[em] the editor
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[CR]build/tsi\f[R] \[em] the tree\-sitter grammar installer
.PP
Then symlink both into \f[CR]\[ti]/.local/bin\f[R] (rebuilds are picked
up automatically \[em] no reinstall needed):
.IP
.EX
make install\-dev
.EE
.PP
For a system\-wide / packaging install instead, \f[CR]make install\f[R]
copies the binaries, man pages and license into an FHS layout under
\f[CR]PREFIX\f[R] (default \f[CR]/usr/local\f[R]), honoring
\f[CR]DESTDIR\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
sudo make install PREFIX=/usr            \f[I]# \-> /usr/bin, /usr/share/man, ...\f[R]
make install PREFIX=/usr DESTDIR=./stage \f[I]# stage for a package\f[R]
.EE
.PP
The extras \[em] portable \f[CR]fzf\f[R]/\f[CR]ripgrep\f[R],
tree\-sitter grammars, and \f[CR]copilot\-language\-server\f[R] (for
\f[CR]:copilot login\f[R]) \[em] are fetched by the one\-line
\f[CR]install.sh\f[R] above, not by the build.
.SS Packages
Homebrew (Linux x86_64):
.IP
.EX
brew tap 42dotmk/hed \f[B]&&\f[R] brew install hed
.EE
.PP
Pre\-built \f[CR].deb\f[R] and \f[CR].rpm\f[R] are attached to each \c
.UR https://github.com/42dotmk/hed/releases/latest
release
.UE \c
, and an \f[CR]apt\f[R]/\f[CR]dnf\f[R] repo is served from GitHub Pages
once enabled (see \f[CR]packaging/\f[R]).
Distro recipes (Arch \f[CR]PKGBUILD\f[R], Void template) and the full
packaging notes \[em] including how to publish to the AUR \[em] live in
\f[CR]packaging/\f[R] too.
.SS Man pages
\f[CR]make man\f[R] generates roff man pages from this README and every
\f[CR]plugins/*/README.md\f[R] (one per plugin) into
\f[CR]man/man1/\f[R] \[em] \f[CR]hed.1\f[R], \f[CR]hed\-tmux.1\f[R],
\f[CR]hed\-vim_keybinds.1\f[R], and so on.
Requires \f[CR]pandoc\f[R].
.PP
The build bakes that path into the binary, so the \f[CR]man\f[R] plugin
can open them from inside the editor with \f[CR]:man hed\f[R],
\f[CR]:man hed\-tmux\f[R], etc.
\[em] no system install needed.
To put them on the system \f[CR]MANPATH\f[R] (so \f[CR]man hed\f[R] /
\f[CR]apropos hed\f[R] work in any shell too):
.IP
.EX
make install\-man        \f[I]# \-> \[ti]/.local/share/man/man1\f[R]
.EE
.PP
