.SH Features
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Modal editing\f[R] (Vim\-style) by default, but also ships
\f[B]Emacs\f[R] and \f[B]VSCode\f[R] keymaps you can swap to at runtime
(\f[CR]:keymap <name>\f[R] to switch, \f[CR]:keymap\-toggle\f[R] to
cycle)
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Tree\-sitter syntax\f[R] highlighting (with grammar via
\f[CR]dlopen\f[R])
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Fzf\f[R] integration for fuzzy file and command search
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Tmux\f[R] runner pane (to test snippets, open REPLs, etc.)
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]OSC 52\f[R] clipboard (to yank to system clipboard, works over SSH)
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]LSP\f[R] integration (work in progress)
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Split windows\f[R], \f[B]reloads\f[R], \f[B]sessions\f[R]
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Git\f[R], \f[B]mail\f[R], \f[B]AI shell\f[R], \f[B]file
manager\f[R] (Yazi)
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Auto\-save\f[R], \f[B]auto\-recover\f[R], \f[B]backup\f[R],
\f[B]undo/redo\f[R]
.PP
   *   *   *   *   *
.SH Why
Hed is for you if:
.IP \[bu] 2
You like to read documentation, not just code
.IP \[bu] 2
You want a single self\-contained binary (links only \f[CR]libdl\f[R];
the tree\-sitter runtime is statically vendored in).
Tools like \f[CR]fzf\f[R], \f[CR]ripgrep\f[R], and \f[CR]tmux\f[R] are
optional and only used when present
.IP \[bu] 2
You like to hack on your editor, not just use it
.IP \[bu] 2
You are a \f[B]plugin developer\f[R] or \f[B]plugin consumer\f[R]
.IP \[bu] 2
You want to \f[B]reinvent the editor\f[R] or \f[B]tune your own\f[R]
.PP
The editor was built for one thing: to be a framework and a template,
not a feature\-rich text editor.
.PP
