.SH Configuration
Config lives in two layers, both compiled in:
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Base config\f[R] \[em] \f[CR]src/config.h\f[R], shipped in\-tree.
It defines the stock plugin manifest
(\f[CR]config_load_default_plugins()\f[R]) and the default theme +
leader keybinds (\f[CR]config_load_defaults()\f[R]).
Edit this to change or remove stock plugins.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]User config\f[R] \[em] \f[CR]\[ti]/.config/hed/config.c\f[R],
optional and user\-owned.
If present, the Makefile compiles it in and runs it \f[I]after\f[R] the
defaults, so it\[cq]s purely additive: enable extra plugins, and
override any keybind via last\-write\-wins.
.PP
A user config just needs to define \f[CR]config_user_init()\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
\f[I]/* \[ti]/.config/hed/config.c */\f[R]
#include \f[B]\[dq]hed.h\[dq]\f[R]

\f[B]extern\f[R] const Plugin plugin_myplugin;   \f[I]/* from EXTRA_PLUGIN_DIRS */\f[R]

void config_user_init(void) {
  plugin_load(&plugin_myplugin, 1);    \f[I]// 1 = enabled, 0 = swappable\f[R]

  \f[I]// Personal overrides \[em] last\-write\-wins, beats plugin defaults.\f[R]
  cmapn(\[dq] ff\[dq], \[dq]recent\[dq], \[dq]recent files\[dq]);
}
.EE
.PP
After editing either layer, run \f[CR]:reload\f[R] to rebuild and
restart.
.SH Keybindings
All keybindings are user\-overridable.
Default is:
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[CR]:keymap\f[R] shows the current keymap; \f[CR]:keymap <name>\f[R]
switches to Vim / Emacs / VSCode, and \f[CR]:keymap\-toggle\f[R] cycles
through them
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[CR]:plugins\f[R] to list currently loaded plugins
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[CR]:reload\f[R] to rebuild and exec the new binary
.PP
   *   *   *   *   *
.SH FAQ
.SS Can I use this with a LSP?
Yes.
The LSP client is in \f[CR]plugins/lsp/\f[R] and is not yet enabled by
default.
.SS How do I override a keybinding?
In your user config (\f[CR]\[ti]/.config/hed/config.c\f[R]) or in
\f[CR]src/config.h\f[R]\[cq]s \f[CR]config_load_defaults()\f[R], use
\f[CR]cmapn(\[dq] key\[dq], \[dq]command\[dq])\f[R] to override or map
keys.
Later registrations win, so a user\-config binding beats the stock
default.
.SS How do I write my own plugin?
See the \f[CR]plugins/example/README.md\f[R] to get started.
.PP
